WEBVTT

00:00.050 --> 00:08.180
Now we want to transition to talking about exponents and an exponent is a little number that we write

00:08.180 --> 00:11.510
in the upper right hand corner of some base.

00:11.510 --> 00:20.690
So in this expression here we have the base three and we say raised to the exponent of two, or we say

00:20.690 --> 00:25.610
this is three to the power of 2 or 3 to the 2 or 3 squared.

00:25.610 --> 00:28.220
Those are all different ways of saying the same thing.

00:28.220 --> 00:32.570
But either way, three is the base and two is the exponent.

00:32.570 --> 00:39.380
What this exponent tells us is that we are supposed to multiply three by itself two times.

00:39.380 --> 00:42.950
In other words, we're supposed to multiply two factors of three.

00:42.950 --> 00:47.330
So the exponent, the value of the exponent tells us the number of factors.

00:47.330 --> 00:51.770
So we could rewrite this expression as three.

00:52.530 --> 00:58.170
Times three, because you can see here that we have two factors of the base three.

00:58.170 --> 01:01.670
And so this is then equal to nine.

01:01.680 --> 01:08.490
So three to the power of 2 or 3 to the exponent of two, three squared is equal to nine.

01:08.790 --> 01:14.820
On the other hand, if we have the opposite situation here, we have the base of two and the exponent

01:14.820 --> 01:15.810
of three.

01:15.840 --> 01:21.030
This tells us to multiply together three factors of the base.

01:21.030 --> 01:27.030
Two So we would rewrite this as two times, two times two.

01:27.030 --> 01:30.660
And we know that two times two is four and four times two is eight.

01:30.660 --> 01:33.060
And so the result here is eight.

01:33.060 --> 01:40.260
So two to the power of 3 or 2 to the exponent of three, or we could call this two cubed is equal to

01:40.260 --> 01:40.920
eight.

01:40.950 --> 01:48.480
So exponents really just give us a shorthand way of writing what would otherwise be an expanded product.

01:48.510 --> 01:56.620
You can see how as these products get larger or if we have five to the power of 4 or 5 to the fourth

01:56.620 --> 01:59.590
power, we would rewrite that as five times.

01:59.590 --> 02:02.740
Five times five times five.

02:02.770 --> 02:07.540
This expression starts to get pretty tedious and a lot to write out.

02:07.570 --> 02:11.770
We can abbreviate this much more simply as five to the fourth power.

02:11.800 --> 02:18.910
We can see here that this is equal to 25 times 25 or 625.

02:18.910 --> 02:25.210
And especially if we have a really big expression like this one, it's going to be much easier to use

02:25.210 --> 02:27.790
an exponent to write this expression.

02:27.790 --> 02:30.670
Otherwise, we have to count the number of sevens that we have.

02:30.700 --> 02:37.240
So here, if we see we have one, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine, ten, 11

02:37.240 --> 02:42.180
of them, then we can just rewrite this as seven to the power of 11.

02:42.190 --> 02:48.730
We can use the exponent of 11 on the base seven to rewrite this as just seven to the 11th instead of

02:48.730 --> 02:53.860
this whole expanded product here, which is going to be really difficult to read and interpret.

02:53.860 --> 02:56.080
So this is what exponents allow us to do.

02:56.080 --> 03:02.110
They allow us to take something like this which really is just unusable and turn it into something very

03:02.110 --> 03:03.190
simple and clean.

03:03.190 --> 03:06.580
So that's the basic idea behind an exponent.

03:06.610 --> 03:11.890
Keep in mind that we can really make the base whatever we want and the exponent whatever we want.

03:11.920 --> 03:14.290
So here's a different kind of example.

03:14.320 --> 03:20.560
Here we have a negative number for the base and then we have a positive three for the exponent.

03:20.560 --> 03:26.290
So this three just tells us to create a product with three factors of negative two.

03:26.320 --> 03:32.830
The fact that we have parentheses around this negative two tells us to apply the three to the entire

03:32.830 --> 03:42.580
negative two so we can rewrite this as negative two times negative two times negative two, three factors

03:42.580 --> 03:43.710
of negative two.

03:43.720 --> 03:48.490
And if we want to simplify this expression, we can say negative two times.

03:48.490 --> 03:50.800
A negative two is a positive four.

03:50.800 --> 03:52.600
So we have four there.

03:52.600 --> 03:59.320
And then still one factor of negative two to deal with four times negative two, of course, is negative

03:59.320 --> 03:59.860
eight.

03:59.860 --> 04:06.520
And so negative two, when we apply the exponent of three to the whole thing gives us a result of negative

04:06.520 --> 04:07.000
eight.

04:07.120 --> 04:13.930
On the other hand, we should know that when we don't have parentheses around the entire negative two

04:13.930 --> 04:18.700
and we instead have this expression, it obviously looks very similar to this one.

04:18.700 --> 04:25.120
But what this tells us is that the exponent of three only applies to the base two, not the negative

04:25.120 --> 04:25.450
sign.

04:25.450 --> 04:32.290
It's almost like we could put parentheses here so that we can see just to apply the three to the base

04:32.290 --> 04:32.980
two.

04:33.010 --> 04:38.380
So this would be equal to we would keep the negative sign out in front.

04:38.380 --> 04:41.440
And then we just have three factors of the base.

04:41.440 --> 04:41.710
Two.

04:41.740 --> 04:43.150
So two times.

04:43.150 --> 04:45.040
Two times two.

04:45.070 --> 04:46.000
This way.

04:46.120 --> 04:48.730
Well, two times two times two is eight.

04:48.730 --> 04:51.700
So we end up with just negative eight.

04:51.700 --> 04:56.890
It's the same result as we got before, but the steps we took to get there actually had to be different.

04:56.890 --> 04:58.480
And that won't always be the case.

04:58.510 --> 05:07.420
Think about it this way If we have negative three to the power of 2 or -3 to the power of two, in this

05:07.420 --> 05:13.090
situation, we have negative three times negative three or.

05:13.680 --> 05:14.980
Positive nine.

05:15.000 --> 05:16.110
But here.

05:16.920 --> 05:18.420
We have negative.

05:18.420 --> 05:22.260
And then this exponent of two applies only to the base three, not the negative sign.

05:22.260 --> 05:23.400
So we have negative.

05:24.360 --> 05:26.460
Three times three or.

05:27.610 --> 05:29.860
Negative nine and we get different results.

05:29.860 --> 05:35.680
So depending on whether the parentheses are wrapped around the negative sign or not, tells us whether

05:35.680 --> 05:40.000
or not to apply that exponent to the negative sign as well as the base.

05:40.000 --> 05:45.010
When we have the parentheses around the negative sign and that base, the exponent applies to the negative

05:45.010 --> 05:47.740
sign as well, not just to the base.

05:47.740 --> 05:54.040
So that's the basic idea of what an exponent is, how we use it to simplify tedious expressions like

05:54.040 --> 06:01.960
this one and how to apply it to the base to find the result by expanding the product.
